          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "फ़सल (fasal) — \"a crop\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Arabic faṣl, whose plain sense is a division or a section — a cut piece of something larger. From there it came to name a season, and from there the thing a season yields."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "North India counts its year in two of them, the winter sowing and the monsoon sowing, so फ़सल (fasal) names the harvest and the stretch of months that produced it at once. Ask a किसान how the फ़सल (fasal) is and you have asked about the weather, the work and the money together."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Two."
            }
          ]
        },
