          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "अनाज (anāj) — \"grain\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Usually traced to Sanskrit अन्न (anna), 'food', through a longer form meaning 'the food that is to be eaten'. The word for food narrowed onto the one food everything else is built around."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "अनाज (anāj) is grain in the bulk sense — what is stored, weighed and sold. चावल is one kind of it, wheat is another, and अनाज (anāj) is the sack all of them come out of."
            }
          ]
        },
