          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "घास (ghās) — \"grass\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Sanskrit घास (ghāsa), 'fodder', on the root घस् (ghas-), 'to eat'. Grass is named from the eating end: it is not a plant, it is what an animal is given."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "That is still how the word behaves. Cut घास (ghās) travels home on a head or a bicycle for the भैंस and the गाय, and the lawn sense — grass you keep and do not feed to anything — is the newer, city meaning laid on top."
            }
          ]
        },
