        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: कुआँ",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "कुआँ (kuā̃) — \"a well\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "From Sanskrit कूप (kūpa), 'a pit, a well'. The p softened away and the vowel came through the nose, leaving a word you write with the moon-and-dot you learnt in the letters chapter."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "कूप has cousins a long way west: Latin cūpa, a tub or a cask, is the same ancient word, and English cup and coop come down from it. A hole in the ground and a thing you drink out of, both named for being hollow."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Five: बीज (bīj), फ़सल (fasal), अनाज (anāj), घास (ghās), कुआँ (kuā̃). Enough to name a field and the water that keeps it."
            }
          ]
        },
